    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "16 The Way, Meadowvale (approx. 98.1 sqm / 1,056 sq ft) is a well-presented three-bedroom semi-detached family home occupying a desirable corner site within the popular Meadowvale development. The property benefits from bright and practical accommodation throughout, together with an extra-large rear garden, off-street parking, side access, and additional attic storage.\r\nThe ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance hall with tiled flooring and carpeted stairs, a comfortable living room with laminate flooring and feature marble fireplace incorporating a solid fuel stove, and a spacious kitchen fitted with a range of units and appliances including an electric hob, oven with grill, dishwasher, and fridge freezer. A convenient guest WC and utility area, plumbed for a washing machine, completes the ground floor accommodation.\r\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms, including a main bedroom with built-in wardrobe and en-suite. The remaining bedrooms offer bright and versatile accommodation, while the family bathroom is fitted with a bath, WC, and WHB. The landing also provides access via Stira stairs to the attic, offering valuable additional storage space.\r\nThe property has a B BER rating, providing good energy efficiency and potential eligibility for a range of green mortgage products, subject to the terms and criteria of individual lenders.\r\nA particular feature of the property is its corner site position, which provides an extra-large rear garden. The front of the property features a concrete driveway providing off-street parking and a lawn area, with side access leading to the rear. The spacious rear garden is laid out with a decking area and lawn, while a garden shed provides additional outdoor storage.\r\nMeadowvale is a popular residential development conveniently located within easy reach of Arklow town and its wide range of shops, schools, supermarkets, public transport links, and local amenities. The property also benefits from convenient access to the M11 motorway.\r\nThis is an excellent opportunity to acquire a spacious three-bedroom family home with an exceptionally generous garden in a convenient and well-established residential location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation\r\nGround Floor\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall\r\n4.51m x 2.66m\r\nTiled flooring. Carpeted stairs.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\n5.44m x 3.37m\r\nLaminate flooring. Feature marble fireplace with solid fuel stove.\r\n\r\nKitchen\r\n4.16m x 5.27m\r\nTiled flooring. Fitted kitchen with electric hob, oven with grill, dishwasher, and fridge freezer.\r\n\r\nWC / Utility Room\r\n2.23m x 1.54m\r\nTiled flooring. Guest WC and WHB. Plumbed for washing machine.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nLanding\r\n2.59m x 1.77m\r\nCarpet flooring. Hot press. Stira stairs to attic storage.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\n4.23m x 3.37m\r\nLaminate flooring. Built-in wardrobe. En-suite.\r\n\r\nEn-Suite\r\n1.73m x 1.80m\r\nTiled flooring. WC. WHB. Electric shower unit.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\n4.43m x 2.56m\r\nLaminate flooring. Built-in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\n4.06m x 2.64m\r\nLaminate flooring.\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\n2.45m x 1.79m\r\nTiled flooring. WC. WHB. Bath."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Eircode Y14 EC99\r\nApprox. 98.1 sqm / 1,056 sq ft\r\nDesirable corner site position with Extra-large rear garden\r\nB BER rating - Potential eligibility for green mortgage products\r\nGas fired central heating\r\nMaster bedroom with en-suite and Built-in wardrobes\r\nAttic storage accessed via Stira stairs\r\nOff-street parking\r\nSide access to rear garden\r\nEasy access to Arklow town and the M11 motorway"
